### Pillar 1: Verified Alumni Directory & Smart Search

#### Flow & Data Model
- **Endpoint**: `GET /api/users`, `GET /api/search`
- **Data Model**: `User` table (`batchYear`, `department`, `currentCompany`, `jobTitle`, `skills`, `isVerified`).
- **Access Control**: Public directory visible to logged-in users; verified badge ($\checkmark$) rendered only if `isVerified === true`.

#### Algorithm: Multi-Attribute Token Matching
When a student types `"CSE 2022 Google React"`, the query parser executes a tokenized weighted search:
$$\text{Query Tokens} = T = \{t_1, t_2, \dots, t_n\}$$
$$\text{Score}(User) = 5 \cdot \mathbb{I}(\text{Company} \in T) + 4 \cdot \mathbb{I}(\text{Role} \in T) + 3 \cdot \mathbb{I}(\text{Batch} \in T) + 2 \cdot \mathbb{I}(\text{Dept} \in T) + 1 \cdot \sum \mathbb{I}(\text{Skill}_i \in T)$$
*Results are sorted by `isVerified DESC, Score DESC, totalPoints DESC`.*

#### Map Visualization (Leaflet.js + OpenStreetMap)
- Users with a `location` field (e.g. `"Bangalore, India"`, `"San Francisco, USA"`) are geocoded using free OpenStreetMap Nominatim.
- Clusters are rendered client-side via Leaflet MarkerCluster with zero external tile subscription fees.

